@carlos-regis Yes, that would be great! And I don't think it will be necessary to include the URI in the message.

We currently repeat the following two lines in at least three different places:
https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/76a4e7507352de5cbabfd8d0130b69012442fe3f/src/Components/Endpoints/src/DependencyInjection/HttpNavigationManager.cs#L14-L15

(e.g., [here](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/76a4e7507352de5cbabfd8d0130b69012442fe3f/src/Components/Server/src/Circuits/RemoteNavigationManager.cs#L90-L91) and [here](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/76a4e7507352de5cbabfd8d0130b69012442fe3f/src/Components/Server/src/Circuits/RemoteNavigationManager.cs#L131-L132))

...So we'll need to update the exception message for each of those call sites.

Maybe we could introduce a [shared source file](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/tree/main/src/Components/Shared/src) containing a helper that converts the given URI string to an absolute URI and throws a `NavigationException` with that URI and the updated message. Something like...

```csharp
// Licensed to the .NET Foundation under one or more agreements.
// The .NET Foundation licenses this file to you under the MIT license.

namespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components;

internal static class NavigationRedirectHelper
{
    private const string RedirectExceptionMessage =
        "A navigation was initiated during static rendering. " +
        "This exception is not an error, but instead signals to the framework that a redirect should occur. " +
        "It should not be caught by application code.";

    [DoesNotReturn]
    public static void ThrowNavigationExceptionForRedirect(NavigationManager navigationManager, string uri)
    {
         var absoluteUriString = ToAbsoluteUri(uri).AbsoluteUri; 
         throw new NavigationException(absoluteUriString, RedirectExceptionMessage); 
    }
}
```

...which we then use at each of the places where we currently throw a `NavigationException`.

(disclaimer: I haven't tried compiling this so the real code may be slightly different)
